WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
Hey guys! I'm Maryna and i'm the designer at

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:02.070
 

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.579
Jungle Scout. I actually designed the

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:04.589
 

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:06.380
Jungle Stix product packaging that

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:06.390
 

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.120
sold almost a hundred thousand dollars

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:08.130
 

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.790
worth of revenue, and today I'm going to

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:10.800
 

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.770
talk about the four tips for your

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:12.780
 

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.049
perfect product packaging! So when you

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:15.059
 

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:16.760
private label, you're going to want to

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:16.770
 

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.650
stand out, so you could dye your hair

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:18.660
 

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.370
pink OR you can follow these four tips!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.380
 

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.529
By default your factory is going to give

00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:24.539
 

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.109
you a generic template, so for a

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:27.119
 

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.519
private label you're going to want

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:28.529
 

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:30.769
something very unique, so make sure that

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:30.779
 

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:33.380
you ask for a template, and also make

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:33.390
 

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.420
sure that it's in the right format, like

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:35.430
 

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.650
a vector, a PDF or EPS. Tip number two - you

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:39.660
 

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.119
have to make sure you've got all the

00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:41.129
 

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:44.119
required info on your product packaging.

00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:44.129
 

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:46.490
The first one is the product origin. For

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:46.500
 

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.170
most of you it's going to be made in

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:48.180
 

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.690
China. Any certifications that you might

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:50.700
 

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.910
have for your product, like FDA approved.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:52.920
 

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.209
If your product comes with a plastic bag,

00:00:56.209 --> 00:00:56.219
 

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:58.130
you must have a suffocation warning

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:58.140
 

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.479
printed on it.

00:00:59.479 --> 00:00:59.489
 

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:00.889
Let's talk about the difference between

00:01:00.889 --> 00:01:00.899
 

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.119
the FNSKU and the UPC. A UPC barcode is

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:05.129
 

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:06.920
something that you see on any product,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:06.930
 

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.760
for example in Walmart. A FNSKU barcode

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:10.770
 

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.670
is a special one that Amazon requires

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:13.680
 

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.310
you to have on your product packaging. So

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:16.320
 

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.050
to save you the trouble of having to

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:18.060
 

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.859
print the FNSKU on top of your UPC, you

00:01:21.859 --> 00:01:21.869
 

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:24.499
can ask your factory to automatically

00:01:24.499 --> 00:01:24.509
 

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:27.230
include it on your product packaging.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:27.240
 

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.840
Pro tip: you wouldn't want to have a

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:29.850
 

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.390
thousand products with the wrong barcode or

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:32.400
 

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.520
one that doesn't scan, so make sure

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:34.530
 

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.980
you double check your proofs. You can do

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:36.990
 

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.230
so by scanning the code on your computer.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:39.240
 

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.710
Just download a barcode scanning app and

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:42.720
 

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.970
off you go! One sec...

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:44.980
 

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.780
So let's talk about the visual design.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:48.790
 

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.960
You can start by researching images that

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:51.970
 

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.510
are related to your product or the ones

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:54.520
 

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.910
that you like. You can then send these

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:56.920
 

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.850
to designers on sites such as Up Work,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:01:59.860
 

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.470
99 Designs or Fiverr. I tend to find that

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:04.480
 

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.770
clean, simple designs, that use one to two

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:07.780
 

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.950
colors are usually the best. Keep in mind

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:10.960
 

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.500
that factories may charge you extra for

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:13.510
 

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.320
multiple colors. The last tip is you want

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:16.330
 

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.080
to add value through your packaging. You

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:19.090
 

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.000
can do so by adding something unique

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.010
 

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.980
that differentiates you from your

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:22.990
 

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.380
competitors. For example, for Jungle

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:25.390
 

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.260
Stix, which are marshmallow sticks, we

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:28.270
 

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.170
used a recipe for delicious smores onto

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:31.180
 

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.360
our label. For you it might be something

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:33.370
 

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.940
different, like a photo of the product

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:35.950
 

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.500
being used in a way that your customers

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:37.510
 

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.660
haven't thought. What you want to keep

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:39.670
 

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.220
in mind is that you want your customers

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:41.230
 

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.220
to have a great first impression.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:44.230
 

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.290
This will encourage them to leave you a

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:46.300
 

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.060
great review and tell their friends

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:48.070
 

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.090
about your product. So remember - ask for a

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:51.100
 

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.820
custom template, include all the required

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:53.830
 

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.510
info including the FNSKU barcode, keep

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:57.520
 

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.420
it clean and simple and add an extra

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:00.430
 

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.760
value for your customers...and don't

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:02.770
 

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:05.910
forget to subscribe!

